## TEE and ZK verification hardening (2026-08-25)

### TEE

- Add `allowed_measurements` to `EnclaveIdentity` and `registered` to `TEEAttestation`.
- `TEEAttestationService._validate_quote` now returns a `QuoteValidationResult`
  distinguishing `verified` (registered enclave, matching public key and
  measurement), `self_consistent` (unregistered but cryptographically signed),
  and `rejected`.
- `verify_and_store` supports `require_registered`; the job-release path uses it.
- Removed the coordinator `auto_attested` quote fallback from `_attach_tee_attestation`.
- A TEE-gated job now releases escrow only when `tee_status == "verified"` and
  the attestation is `registered`.
- Added alembic migration `5d8339a13a12` and updated `test_v024_tee_verification_trust.py`.
- Live: deployed to `hub.aitbc` and `aitbc3`; `aitbc-coordinator-api` restarted.

### ZK

- Added `receipt_model.circom` and built artifacts (`_0001.zkey`, `.wasm`,
  `verification_key.json`) using a phase-2 contribution on the gitea runner.
- `receipt_model` public signals are `input_hash`, `model_hash`, `output_hash`,
  and `model_id`; it proves a committed deterministic model executed on a
  committed input to produce a committed output. It does not prove semantic
  correctness of open-ended text.
- Added `model_registry.py` with one supported deterministic model (`linear-1`).
- Extended `ZKProofService` with `generate_model_proof` and `verify_model_proof`;
  `verify_model_proof` returns `computation_correct=True` only when the proof
  verifies *and* its public signals match the coordinator-derived expected values.
- `receipt_public` remains a receipt-binding artifact; it no longer sets
  `computation_correct` on its own.
- Updated `_attach_zk_proof`: ZK-required jobs must specify a supported model;
  unsupported models fail closed with `computation_correct=False` and
  `zk_status="unsupported_model"`.
- Added `apps/coordinator-api/tests/test_receipt_model.py` and updated
  `test_zk_receipt.py` to reflect that `receipt_public` verification does not
  imply computation correctness.
- Updated `.pre-commit-config.yaml` to exempt generated `.wasm` binaries from
  the large-file size gate.
- Live: circuit artifacts and coordinator code pushed to Gitea from `aitbc3`;
  deployment to `hub.aitbc` is pending recovery of the hub node.
